From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homescoop <homescoop@ai-ecoverse.invalid>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wasi: homescoop's allocator refresh as the global allocator

V8 checks a thread's memory.fill/memory.copy against that thread's cached
memory length, which can lag a memory.grow another thread's malloc just
did, so a memset into a fresh block traps "memory access out of bounds"
(slicc-kernel#1172, homescoop#1287). On wasm the uv binary includes
scripts/rust-wasm-refresh-alloc.rs (path in HOMESCOOP_WASM_ALLOC_RS, set by
build.sh): System, refreshing the view with memory.grow(0) before a block
above it is returned. uv's own allocator crate picks nothing on wasm32.
---
 crates/uv/src/bin/uv.rs | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/uv/src/bin/uv.rs b/crates/uv/src/bin/uv.rs
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/crates/uv/src/bin/uv.rs
+++ b/crates/uv/src/bin/uv.rs
@@ -7,6 +7,15 @@ extern crate uv_performance_memory_allocator;
 
 use std::process::ExitCode;
 
+// homescoop#1287: threaded wasm takes homescoop's allocator refresh
+// (scripts/rust-wasm-refresh-alloc.rs) against V8's stale per-thread memory
+// length after another thread's memory.grow.
+#[cfg(target_family = "wasm")]
+#[allow(unsafe_code)]
+mod homescoop_wasm_alloc {
+    include!(env!("HOMESCOOP_WASM_ALLOC_RS"));
+}
+
 use uv::main as uv_main;
 
 #[allow(unsafe_code)]
